{"name":"Agapanthus","hex":"#bbc5de","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Agapanthus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Amaryllidaceae – certain flowering plants of South Africa, some called African lily or lily of the Nile."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Agapanthus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Agapanthus","blocks":[{"text":"Agapanthus is a genus of plants, the only one in the subfamily Agapanthoideae of the family Amaryllidaceae. The subfamily was formerly treated as a separate family, Agapanthaceae. The family is in the monocot order Asparagales. The name is derived from Ancient Greek ἀγάπη (agápē), meaning \"love\", and ἄνθος (ánthos), meaning \"flower\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Agapanthus_africanus1.jpg/330px-Agapanthus_africanus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agapanthus","wikidata":"Q159541"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG/500px-Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG/1280px-Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG/500px-Agapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Agapanthus flower and leaves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAgapanthus_Flower_and_Leaves.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Agapanthus_africanus_in_habitat_photo_Nick_Helme_CC_by_SA.jpg/500px-Agapanthus_africanus_in_habitat_photo_Nick_Helme_CC_by_SA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or